id: pm-gh1487
title: "GH-1487: Respect nested Git repository boundaries during tracker discovery"
description: Investigate implicit tracker discovery crossing the nearest Git repository boundary and silently mutating an enclosing repository tracker when the nested repository has no tracker. Preserve explicit tracker overrides and intentional workspace policies.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: github-intake,release-closeout
created_at: "2026-10-17T02:29:28.964Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T18:41:50.192Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-17T18:41:49.029Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-17T18:41:49.029Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce in disposable outer/inner Git repositories and verify outer bytes/history remain unchanged on refused inner mutations; cover .git directories and files, worktrees, submodules and ordinary subdirectories; preserve explicit --pm-path and PM_PATH plus documented deliberate cross-root policy; expose actionable boundary and initialization recovery through SDK, CLI and MCP."
definition_of_ready: Live duplicate search and canonical lineage reviewed; reported evidence retained; implementation must first reproduce in isolated fixtures and keep existing gates.
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Implicit discovery stops at the nearest Git root, including .git files for worktrees/submodules, with clear initialization recovery; deliberate tracker overrides remain supported."
value: "Preserve reliable, economical project context and explicit evidence across repositories and tool integrations."
why_now: New live GitHub report or integration observation arrived during verified2026.10.17 release closeout.
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
severity: high
resolution: "Implicit discovery follows physical directory ancestry, preserves missing initialization suffixes, stops at Git directories/gitfiles, and propagates unexpected lookup failures. Explicit tracker selection and initialized tracker-layout precedence remain supported."
expected_result: "Nested checkout, worktree, submodule and directory-alias operations must not implicitly mutate outer trackers; recovery remains local and deliberate cross-root selection remains possible."
actual_result: "All31 focused controls and all3 governed linked commands pass, including four reviewer regressions that failed before remediation. Real SDK/CLI/MCP and packed npm/Bun consumers preserve outer bytes, refuse implicit nested writes and initialize locally; npx/bunx dispatch succeeds. Unchanged local startup-budget refusal remains separately tracked; final hosted checks are required before merge."
component: workspace tracker discovery
